/**
@mainpage vkmEngine API Reference

The generated reference for the types a project compiles against. It is not the manual:
[the manual](https://vkmengine.com/docs/) says how each subsystem works and what the
engine holds to, and is the better place to start.

@section api_where Where to look first

| If you are | Start at |
|------------|----------|
| Writing gameplay | Vkm::Engine::Behavior, Vkm::Engine::BehaviorContext |
| Building a world in code | Vkm::Engine::Scene, Vkm::Engine::EntityId |
| Loading or making assets | Vkm::Engine::ResourceManager, Vkm::Engine::Handle |
| Reacting to things | Vkm::Engine::EventBus, Vkm::Engine::FrameContext |
| Writing a system | Vkm::Engine::System, Vkm::Engine::SystemStage |

@section api_conventions Conventions worth knowing before you read anything

- **Forward is -Z, screen-right is +X, up is +Y** - right-handed, glm's own convention.
  Ask through Vkm::Engine::Math::computeForward and friends.
- **Components are plain structs.** Storing one needs no registration and no base class;
  saving one needs a reflect block and a row in `VKM_SCENE_COMPONENTS`, and replicating
  one Vkm::Engine::NetSchema::replicate.
- **Assets are referenced by Vkm::Engine::Handle, never by pointer**, and serialized by
  *name* - the name is the identity that survives a save.
- **Systems talk through Vkm::Engine::FrameContext**, not by holding each other:
  references are services, pointers are per-frame products, null until their producer
  has run, but for `debug`, a service a host may not keep. The editor's
  `EditorSystem`, which drives the engine, is the one system that holds others.

@section api_stability What is stable

Everything under `Vkm::Engine` that a project can include is public surface, and so
are `Vkm::Platform`, `Vkm::Audio`, `Vkm::Network` and `Vkm::Physics`: vkmPlatform,
vkmAudio, vkmNetwork and vkmPhysics, the engine's libraries, each versioned
separately. Anything in a `detail` namespace is not public and will move without
notice.
*/
